---
import PublicPage from '../layouts/PublicPage.astro';

const updated = 'April 28, 2026';
const canonical = 'https://usdwatch.com/ai-disclosure/';
const description = 'How USDWatch uses AI, model providers, evidence extraction, vector search, and human review.';
const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'USDWatch AI Disclosure',
    url: canonical,
    dateModified: '2026-04-27',
    description,
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'USDWatch',
      url: 'https://usdwatch.com/',
    },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Is USDWatch just ChatGPT?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'No. USDWatch uses a multi-step workflow around AI models: intake reading, evidence extraction, retrieval and vector search, gap analysis, and self-advocacy packet synthesis.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Does AI train on my private case?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'USDWatch does not build or train a custom public model from a private case file. The product may store structured outputs, extracted text, embeddings, logs, Case Reads, and packet artifacts needed to operate the workspace.',
        },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Can AI output be wrong?',
        acceptedAnswer: {
          '@type': 'Answer',
          text: 'Yes. AI may miss context, sound too certain, or misunderstand facts. USDWatch output is informational preparation and should not be treated as legal advice or final authority.',
        },
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<PublicPage
  title="USDWatch AI Disclosure"
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 sm:py-16 space-y-12 animate-fade-up">
    <section class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent font-semibold">AI Disclosure</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight">
        This is not just a chat box pointed at your story.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-dim">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
        USDWatch uses AI to help organize messy school-district facts into a working case file. The goal is not to make a legal decision for you. The goal is to help you understand evidence strength, gaps, records to request, meeting questions, and next steps.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/login" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-md bg-accent text-background text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-accent-hover transition-colors">
          Start My Case
        </a>
        <a href="/privacy" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-md border border-border text-sm font-semibold text-text hover:bg-surface-alt transition-colors">
          Privacy & Disclosures
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-bold">Multiple steps</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
          A Case Read runs through intake, evidence extraction, records research, gap analysis, and final synthesis. It is not a single generic prompt.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-bold">Purpose-built agents</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
          Agent workers focus on different jobs: reading intake, extracting evidence, identifying key date anchors, finding missing records, and drafting practical next steps.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-bold">Private by default</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
          Your case is scoped to your workspace. Attorney, advocacy, media, or parent-group routing is manual opt-in only.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[280px_1fr]">
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Is this just ChatGPT?</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">Short answer: no.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
          USDWatch can use large language models, but the product is the workflow around them: evidence intake, document parsing, structured schemas, model routing, agent run persistence, workspace isolation, and packet generation.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
          A general chatbot waits for you to know what to ask. USDWatch tries to ask the case-file questions for you: what happened, what evidence supports it, what is missing, what records could confirm it, and what a parent can do next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-5">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">How the AI pipeline works</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4">
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">1. Intake reading</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            The system reads your Case Advocate conversation and draft facts panel: impacted person context, age or grade band, issue categories, urgency, safety concerns, retaliation concerns, prior actions, and desired outcomes.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">2. Evidence extraction</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            Uploaded documents and explicitly imported Gmail evidence in the Evidence Locker are parsed when possible. The system looks for dates, actors, claims, decisions, notices, records, policy references, and inconsistencies.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">3. Retrieval and vector search</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            We may convert document text into embeddings and store them in a vector database so related passages can be found later. That is not the same as training a new neural network on your case. It is more like creating a searchable evidence map.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">4. Gap analysis</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            The system compares the story and available evidence against the kinds of records a parent would usually need: communications, incident reports, policies, meeting notes, IEP or 504 records, agency letters, and key date anchors.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">5. Self-Advocacy Packet</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            The output is a packet: case summary, key dates, evidence checklist, records request drafts, meeting questions, escalation options, and next-step plan. It is informational, not legal advice.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[280px_1fr]">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Models and providers</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-3">
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            USDWatch is built to route different jobs to different models. Cheaper, faster models can handle extraction and classification. Stronger reasoning models can handle deeper review and synthesis. The configured stack uses DeepInfra-hosted NVIDIA/Nemotron-family models, with a DeepInfra-hosted Llama fallback when needed.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            The current USDWatch pipeline is not routed to Gemini or Anthropic. Model choices can still change as quality, cost, and privacy options improve, but model use should be purposeful: send the minimum useful context needed for the job, then return structured outputs that the app can display and test.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[280px_1fr]">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">How your data is used with AI</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5">
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
          <li>Relevant intake answers and document text may be sent to AI/model providers so they can process the Case Advocate conversation, Case Read, and packet outputs.</li>
          <li>If you connect Gmail, only matched/imported messages and attachments become Evidence Locker content for AI processing.</li>
          <li>Generated outputs are stored in your workspace as Case Reads, evidence gaps, recommended records, and packet artifacts.</li>
          <li>Evidence Locker files remain private to your workspace unless you explicitly choose to share a limited summary for support review.</li>
          <li>Support outreach is not automated. Opting in creates a manual review path; it does not publish your case or automatically send it to attorneys, media, or advocacy groups.</li>
          <li>We do not use AI output as a final legal, educational, disciplinary, medical, or safety decision about a child.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[280px_1fr]">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">What AI can get wrong</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-4">
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">It can miss context.</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            AI may misunderstand school jargon, family history, disability context, state-specific rules, or the difference between a rumor and a document-backed fact.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">It can sound too certain.</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            USDWatch tries to show evidence strength, confidence, and gaps so the output does not read like a legal conclusion.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">It cannot replace professional judgment.</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            A qualified attorney, advocate, clinician, or emergency professional may see issues that a Case Read misses. Use USDWatch as preparation, not as final authority.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-5">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Questions parents usually ask</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">Does AI train on my private case?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            USDWatch does not build or train a custom public model from your case file. The product may store structured outputs, extracted text, embeddings, logs, Case Reads, and packet artifacts needed to operate your workspace.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">Can I use the output as a complaint?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            Treat it as a working draft and checklist. Before filing anything formal, review the facts, attach source records, and consider qualified legal or advocacy help.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">Will a human see my case?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            Normal Case Reads are automated. Human review may happen for support, safety, security, operations, abuse prevention, or if you opt into attorney, advocacy, media, or parent-group support.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">Why disclose this much?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
            Families are uploading sensitive facts. You deserve to know when AI is involved, what it is doing, and where the limits are.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-lg p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Standards we pay attention to</h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-dim">
        AI disclosure expectations are becoming normal. We watch consumer-protection guidance, AI risk-management frameworks, and transparency rules as they evolve.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm">
        <a class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover" href="https://www.ftc.gov/industry/technology/artificial-intelligence" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FTC AI consumer-protection work</a>
        <a class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover" href="https://www.nist.gov/itl/ai-risk-management-framework" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NIST AI Risk Management Framework</a>
        <a class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover" href="https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/faqs/navigating-ai-act" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">EU AI Act transparency overview</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</PublicPage>
